<Project>
  <!-- Methodology audit (plans/methodology-audit-2026-06-25.md, item 2).

       NuGet vulnerability auditing: the build now surfaces NU1901-1904 for
       known-CVE direct AND transitive packages (a VPN client's crypto / parsing
       / HTTP dependency surface). Warning-level by design - it informs without
       blocking the build; pair with Dependabot alerts (audit item 6).

       DENY-WARNINGS is intentionally NOT enabled here yet. The Release build
       currently carries ~194 warnings (incl. ~68 CS8602 null-deref). Flipping
       them to errors at the root would break every build immediately. The
       burndown - fix the warnings, then enable <TreatWarningsAsErrors> (or a
       <WarningsAsErrors> subset) - is tracked as a follow-up in the audit plan
       (P0 item 2). Adding the props file now makes that flip a one-line change
       once the backlog is clear. -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <NuGetAudit>true</NuGetAudit>
    <NuGetAuditMode>all</NuGetAuditMode>
    <NuGetAuditLevel>moderate</NuGetAuditLevel>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
